{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469423-looking-for-advice-on-running-a-lasombra-court-of-blood","id":1469423,"title":"Looking for advice on running a Lasombra Court of Blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-02T15:22:26-08:00","id":1469423,"title":"Looking for advice on running a Lasombra Court of Blood","content":"So I'm prepping to run a Lasombra Court of Blood for one of the PCs in the Dark Ages game I'm running. Using evidence they've gathered, along with witnesses that have agreed to speak before the court, the PC is going to charge Narses (Prince of Venice) with spearheading a plot to bring down Michael and the Cainites of Constantinople.<br /> <br /> I believe the basic accusation the PC plans to make is that Narses pursued a personal vendetta with Michael and the other Cainites of Constantinople, setting in motion a series of events that led to the Latin Riots of 1185, which resulted in the death of nearly every Cainite in the Latin Quarter of Constantinople, the Fourth Crusade and the attempted sacking of Constantinople (they were actually able to stop Constantinople from being completely sacked) and a number of other events that if discovered, would risk war between the Lasombra and the Cainites of Constantinople, including the methuselah Toreador Michael (I should add that the PCs managed to save Michael and his childer from dying, along with a good many others).<br /> <br /> I'm looking for suggestions on running the actual trial itself at the table. What questions do you think the judges might ask, perhaps to clarify or poke holes in things the PC presents? What parts do you think would interesting to RP through, and what would you leave to summary and dice rolls?<br /> <br /> In case it matters, here's some of the evidence and witnesses that are set to testify.<br /> <br /> <b>Hard Evidence</b><br /> <b>Written Correspondence</b><br /> The written correspondence between Narses and his childe Alfonzo concerning the plan against Constantinople that\u2019s written in code. Currently being deciphered by the Nosferatu Mouse.<br /> <br /> <b>The Stake</b><br /> The blood coated stake used to incapacitate the Ventrue Epirus, who\u2019d arranged the Latin Riots of 1185 C.E. as a favor to the Lasombra Alfonzo, childe of Narses.<br /> <br /> <b>Alfonzo\u2019s Letter to Magdalena</b><br /> A letter from Alfonzo to Magdalena containing Alfonzo\u2019s account of Narses\u2019 involvement in the Latin Riots of 1185.<br /> <br /> <b>Witnesses</b><br /> <b>Gabriella of Genoa</b><br /> Gabriella is aware of Alfonzo\u2019s meetings with the Malkavian Gregorius, and that Gregorius was slowly and secretly driving Michael into a state of madness at the behest of Alfonzo.<br /> <br /> <b>Gu\u00f0brandr</b><br /> Witnessed three Ventrue Methuselahs attend one of Alfonzo's blood feasts. Gu\u00f0brandr can attest that the three Methuselahs and Alfonzo temporarily left the party together to discuss some matter in private. The PC claims to have witnessed the discussion between Alfonzo and the methuselahs, during which they acknowledged they were aware of a plan between Narses and Alfonzo to destroy Michael and the Cainite leadership of Constantinople. Alfonzo had expected the methuselahs to aid in the plan, but they explained they themselves would not get involved, and were merely there to bear witness to monumental events of historical significance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T00:58:21-08:00","id":1469470,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong, and maybe this is just a modern nights thing, but aren't the Lasombra courts of blood mostly concerned about killing Lasombra that bring down the brand rather than any notion of right and wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T10:55:06-08:00","id":1469506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469423-looking-for-advice-on-running-a-lasombra-court-of-blood?p=1469470#post1469470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, and maybe this is just a modern nights thing, but aren't the Lasombra courts of blood mostly concerned about killing Lasombra that bring down the brand rather than any notion of right and wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing things to bring down the brand, put the clan at risk, not living up to your potential as a clan member (getting caught doing something big and stupid, of course it may only be seen as stupid because they got caught). For sure, the court of blood isn\u2019t going to be concerned about the morality of this situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T15:11:11-08:00","id":1469593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469423-looking-for-advice-on-running-a-lasombra-court-of-blood?p=1469506#post1469506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doing things to bring down the brand, put the clan at risk, not living up to your potential as a clan member (getting caught doing something big and stupid, of course it may only be seen as stupid because they got caught). For sure, the court of blood isn\u2019t going to be concerned about the morality of this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which of course is not to say the Court of Blood wouldn't hear the case. You just wouldn't be able to convince the court of anything on moral grounds.<br /> <br /> You'd need to convince the court that destroying all of Venice's Kindred, causing a Crusade, and getting Constantinople sacked is somehow not in the interests of Clan Lasombra.<br /> <br /> How exactly that works is up to the Player Characters to argue.<br /> <br /> Which neatly brings us to the OP point: the members of the court are going to ask &quot;Why is this relevant to the court? Why should Clan Lasombra care?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T18:10:35-08:00","id":1469608,"title":"","content":"They'll probably ask questions related to how those actions affected the clan's standing in the region, along with its assets. As a court they'll be judging the accused worth for the clan, but they'll also consider the possible benefits in extending their ties to the accusers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T20:14:35-08:00","id":1469618,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra are called Magisters for a reason \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T14:38:04-08:00","id":1469958,"title":"","content":"In the DA era the Courts of Blood are pretty much church courts, so watch In The Name of the Rose, or read some Roman proceedings like Cicero. depends how hard you want to go, and temper it by what the judges care about, are they Road of the Abyss, or Azaneali, or are they Road of Sin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-08-2021, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T20:01:56-08:00","id":1469994,"title":"","content":"The court should absolve the prince of venice<ul><li>He showcased great ambition and cunning</li> <li>He made a good plan to defeat a powerful ancient and thus a competitor in the grand scheme.</li> <li>He weakened the leadership of constantinople Michael is in torpor wich is a big thing wich means the city could be taken by the LaSombra</li> </ul><br /> I don\u00b4t see how what he did puts the LaSombra clan in a bad position , heck I can see the prince of Venice asking the blood court to make a trial on the party LaSombra clan members for hindering his plans to take over Constantinople for moral reasons instead of helping him expand the clan territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T13:23:27-08:00","id":1470292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469423-looking-for-advice-on-running-a-lasombra-court-of-blood?p=1469994#post1469994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The court should absolve the prince of venice<ul><li>He showcased great ambition and cunning</li> <li>He made a good plan to defeat a powerful ancient and thus a competitor in the grand scheme.</li> <li>He weakened the leadership of constantinople Michael is in torpor wich is a big thing wich means the city could be taken by the LaSombra</li> </ul><br /> I don\u00b4t see how what he did puts the LaSombra clan in a bad position , heck I can see the prince of Venice asking the blood court to make a trial on the party LaSombra clan members for hindering his plans to take over Constantinople for moral reasons instead of helping him expand the clan territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he was discovered. This all may stay being good for the Clan, but can <b>he</b> benefit of it now? What if the party Lasombra have now a better position to leverage this apparent superior morality under the circumstances so produced?<br /> <br /> The Court won't judge based on morality. But it also won't judge based on justice. If throwing the Prince under the carriage is better for the clan, so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T12:28:18-08:00","id":1472253,"title":"","content":"What questions do you think the judges might ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T20:11:03-08:00","id":1472745,"title":"","content":"I think that the judges will first ask Why should He be judged, even though they think it might be possible since they are holding trial after all, and Narses is one big MoFa figure to trial. So they might like to judge and put to execution someone that big in the Clan to show the strenght and importance of the Court, also, he was discovered, which is very bad.<br /> <br /> In the end it is as has been said by others here, they will want to know what he is being accused of, the crimes are only according to 'does it hurt/benefit the Clan', 'how does this balances power in the Clan', 'is his unlife/death beneficial to us'... and if the basis of the accusation are founded (which seem to be the most important part on the Court of Blood) we go to the second most important thing, that is the evidence (and yeah, it is mostly secondary, but important). So, the PCs gotta appeal to the judges.<br /> <br /> It would be very good if they stated how much bad rep Narses is bringing down on Lasombra, which might stick to other members, especially because he messed up with three godlike figures that hold great sway on three High Clans on the most important city in Europe, for simply petty revenge, and got caught (and started the War of Princes, which might be something Lasombras are fans or not). So yeah, killing him would not only keep the Lasombra clean from the bad actions of Narses (while keeping the aura of what they're capable of), but endear the Clan to those that would take revenge (or not, really). It is also important to know that even more than Lasombra Narses is the Archbishop of the Cainite Heresy, so it would be good for Lasombra-Heresy relations since they end up spurring him, and ending him first would give the Lasombras more respect. <br /> <br /> I think the Courts of Blood are simply the way the Clan of Individuals have to deal selfishly with the individuals that harm the group (which is... every single Lasombra individually). Cuz they really don't care about petty crimes, evildoing, vendettas, sin... only themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}